From: Remy <remy@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: APSS watchdog handoff - disarm at end of device init, or leave armed on request

REVIEW-20261031-2230 F-4: the bootloader arms the APSS
watchdog before handoff (P3: wdt dev + wdt start in the
U-Boot boot command), its hardware fuse is ~32 s (the qcom
driver clamps 300000 ms to its 32003 ms maximum), and
U-Boot's servicing stops at handoff - so unpetted it bites
~32 s into every boot. New module qcom_wdt (feature
qcom-wdt-handoff, default OFF): FDT discovery of the
watchdog@17980000 node (KPSS layout via the compatible
fallback both the fork's U-Boot driver and Linux bind;
APCS-TMR layouts recognized and refused; reg span must
cover the register block), and at the END of device init -
the healthy point - it takes ownership: REDOX_WDT_MODE=leave
(bootloader patch 0006) leaves the watchdog armed for
stall tests; anything else disarms by clearing only the
WDT_EN enable bit (read-modify-write, readback-verified).
Fail-safe throughout: a failed disarm warns and boots on,
and patch 0042 makes even that bite land in the normal boot
path. No petting in this patch. Host tests 9/9 (layout
selection, env parsing, EN math, disarm/leave transactions).

